{"content":[{"c":["JEHIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. KJV spelling of Jeiel, King Saul’s ancestor, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.35","r":"1Chr.9.35","rawR":"1Chr.9.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.35","value":"1Chr.9.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 9:35"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jeiel #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. KJV spelling of Jeiel, Hotham’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.44","r":"1Chr.11.44","rawR":"1Chr.11.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.44","value":"1Chr.11.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 11:44"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jeiel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jeiel #3"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. A Levite musician who, along with other Levites appointed by David, played a psaltery at the removal of the ark to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18-20","r":"1Chr.15.18-20","rawR":"1Chr.15.18-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18-20","value":"1Chr.15.18-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:18-20"},"). Afterward, he was appointed to a permanent ministry of music in the sanctuary (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","r":"1Chr.16.5","rawR":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.5","value":"1Chr.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Levite of the family of Gershon; a chief of the house of Ladan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.8","r":"1Chr.23.8","rawR":"1Chr.23.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.8","value":"1Chr.23.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:8"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). He was in charge of the temple treasury during David’s reign—an office that seems to have continued in the family (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.29.8","r":"1Chr.29.8","rawR":"1Chr.29.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.29.8","value":"1Chr.29.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"29:8"},")—and founder of a priestly family called Jehieli or Jehielites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.21-22","r":"1Chr.26.21-22","rawR":"1Chr.26.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.21-22","value":"1Chr.26.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:21-22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Hacmoni’s son who, with David’s uncle Jonathan (a counselor and a scribe), was appointed to take care of the king’s sons as a tutor and adviser (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.32","r":"1Chr.27.32","rawR":"1Chr.27.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.32","value":"1Chr.27.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:32"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Son of King Jehoshaphat of Judah, placed by his father over one of the fortified cities of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.21.2","r":"2Chr.21.2","rawR":"2Chr.21.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.21.2","value":"2Chr.21.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 21:2"},"). He and five brothers were slain by Jehoram when Jehoram became king."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. One of the Kohathite Levites from the family of Heman who assisted in King Hezekiah’s reforms (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.14","r":"2Chr.29.14","rawR":"2Chr.29.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.14","value":"2Chr.29.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:14"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Jehuel”). He may be the same Levite who was assigned to oversee the reception and distribution of the sacred offerings (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.31.13","r":"2Chr.31.13","rawR":"2Chr.31.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.31.13","value":"2Chr.31.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 31:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. One of the chief officers of the temple at the time of Josiah’s religious reformation (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.8","r":"2Chr.35.8","rawR":"2Chr.35.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.8","value":"2Chr.35.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:8"},"); he contributed many sacrifices for the great Passover service."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Father of Obadiah from Joab’s house; he returned with Ezra from Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.9","r":"Ezra.8.9","rawR":"Ezra.8.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.9","value":"Ezra.8.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the sons of Elam and father of Shecaniah. He was associated with Ezra’s marriage reforms (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.2","r":"Ezra.10.2","rawR":"Ezra.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.2","value":"Ezra.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:2"},") and was perhaps the same Jehiel who was among those who divorced their foreign wives (v ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.26","r":"Ezra.10.26","rawR":"Ezra.10.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.26","value":"Ezra.10.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Priest who was among those Ezra persuaded to divorce their foreign wives (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.21","r":"Ezra.10.21","rawR":"Ezra.10.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.21","value":"Ezra.10.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jehiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 9:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.35","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.35","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.35"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 11:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.44","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.44","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.44"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:18-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.18-20","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.18-20","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.18-20"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 23:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.23.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.23.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.23.8"},{"anchorText":"29:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.29.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.29.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.29.8"},{"anchorText":"26:21-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.21-22","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.21-22","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.21-22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.32","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.32","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.32"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 21:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.21.2","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.21.2","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.21.2"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 31:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.31.13","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.31.13","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.31.13"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 35:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.35.8","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.35.8","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.35.8"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.9","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.9","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.9"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.2"},{"anchorText":"26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.26","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.26","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.26"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.21","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.21","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"09ce92ca9c85122f681741df7d0e816563a693ff629142c1e2d412fa2ba059f9","sourceItemName":"Jehiel","sourceItemOrder":139,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jehiel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jehiel","title":"Jehiel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}